index_scores.cu   from zig/kernels/cuda/glm_index_scores.cuh (tf_glm_index_scores)
index_header.cu   from zig/kernels/cuda/common/cp_async.cuh, common/qmm_frag.cuh
                  and glm_index_scores.cuh (the cp.async, ldmatrix and mma
                  wrappers and the tile layout)

Changes: the kernel is the body of an mx.fast.cuda_kernel instead of a
precompiled function. Sizes come from the input shapes and template
arguments. The head weights arrive already scaled, and the dot products are
not scaled. Each score is rounded once to bf16, and a pooled window that is
not complete at the query position gets the bf16 value of -1e30 instead of
-inf, which is what the oMLX host hands its top-k selection. Paged key
storage is dropped.
Each tensor-core step sums its 16 products from zero and the sum is added
to the float32 accumulator rounded to nearest.
